Description: Separate full-screen setup for Kernora OS
 Kernora runs the installer as its own full-screen setup before the desktop
 starts, drawn like the Pixel setup wizard:
  - a branding with windowExpanding: fullscreen shows a real full-screen
    window instead of a maximized one;
  - leaving from the first page (Try without installing) quits without the
    cancel question, nothing has been chosen there yet;
  - QML pages can store their choices with Global.insert / Global.remove;
  - the zones model tells QML the region of each zone;
  - the install page hides its own progress bar and log button and writes
    the progress to the global storage (kernoraProgress, kernoraProgressMessage)
    so the slideshow draws it;
  - the partition page sits in the same Pixel frame as the QML pages: back
    button, title and text on the left, the choices on the right and the
    Next button at the bottom, because the window has no navigation bar.
Author: Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-19
